WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
An investigation begins with a decision, not a verdict.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.780
In this synthetic case, we want to distinguish one operator from

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.169
shared infrastructure. Pivotglass keeps the question, the

00:00:10.169 --> 00:00:13.559
evidence, and alternative explanations together. Novice

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:16.881
coaching starts simply: What data do you have? What happened?

00:00:16.881 --> 00:00:20.339
Do you know how it started? Here, we do not. Keep that unknown.

00:00:20.339 --> 00:00:23.729
The coach proposes questions, and the analyst edits one to ask

00:00:23.729 --> 00:00:27.119
what independent evidence would distinguish common control from shared

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:30.508
hosting. Review before saving. Practice records

00:00:30.508 --> 00:00:33.898
participation and reflection; expertise grows through real

00:00:33.898 --> 00:00:37.288
work and feedback. Now preview a local report.

00:00:37.288 --> 00:00:40.678
Candidate strings are separate from admitted evidence. Select the

00:00:40.678 --> 00:00:44.068
domain and long URL, then explicitly admit them with their

00:00:44.068 --> 00:00:47.458
source. The library retains the source digest. A

00:00:47.458 --> 00:00:50.847
successful preview is not admission, and a document claim is not

00:00:50.847 --> 00:00:54.237
automatically true. Open the indicator. Read the complete

00:00:54.237 --> 00:00:57.627
value, typed relationships, original source, and collection history.

00:00:57.627 --> 00:01:01.017
The file communicates with a domain, but topology alone

00:01:01.017 --> 00:01:04.407
does not establish ownership. Keep both hypotheses.

00:01:04.407 --> 00:01:07.797
Record the conflicting explanation and what independent collection

00:01:07.797 --> 00:01:11.186
could resolve it. Link evidence to a hypothesis with an explicit
stance and

00:01:11.186 --> 00:01:14.576
rationale. The competing-hypotheses matrix lets us compare the same

00:01:14.576 --> 00:01:17.966
evidence across alternatives. Then record a structured

00:01:17.966 --> 00:01:21.356
technique run: inputs, analysis, limitations, and

00:01:21.356 --> 00:01:24.746
disposition. Required fields make the work inspectable;

00:01:24.746 --> 00:01:27.729
the analyst still evaluates the argument.

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:31.525
Coverage shows where the investigation has evidence and where it needs
more.

00:01:31.525 --> 00:01:34.915
It does not measure danger. Likelihood asks how

00:01:34.915 --> 00:01:38.305
probable an explanation is. Confidence asks how sound and

00:01:38.305 --> 00:01:41.695
sufficient its evidence and reasoning are. Keep the collection

00:01:41.695 --> 00:01:45.085
requirement and stopping condition visible so the hunt has a purpose
and

00:01:45.085 --> 00:01:48.475
a boundary. Generate the workspace report. Review questions,

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:51.864
alternatives, explicit evidence links, technique results,

00:01:51.864 --> 00:01:55.254
unresolved contradictions, and next steps. Save Markdown for

00:01:55.254 --> 00:01:58.644
an editable handoff, or print to PDF. Before

00:01:58.644 --> 00:02:02.034
sharing, check source handling and limitations. The next analyst

00:02:02.034 --> 00:02:05.424
should be able to reconstruct the case, challenge the judgment, and

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:06.915
continue the work.
